 3. How do you configure TestNG listeners?

There are three common approaches.

Option A — Annotation

import org.testng.annotations.Listeners;
import org.testng.annotations.Test;

@Listeners(ScreenshotListener.class)
public class TransferTests {

    @Test
    public void validTransferTest() {
        // Arrange, execute transfer, and assert result.
    }
}

This is simple for a specific test class.

Option B — testng.xml

<!DOCTYPE suite SYSTEM "https://testng.org/testng-1.0.dtd">
<suite name="Banking Regression">
    <listeners>
        <listener class-name="com.company.reporting.ScreenshotListener"/>
    </listeners>

    <test name="Transfer Tests">
        <classes>
            <class name="com.company.tests.TransferTests"/>
        </classes>
    </test>
</suite>

Use this when you want to apply a listener to a suite without decorating every test class.

Option C — Programmatic registration

import org.testng.TestNG;

TestNG testng = new TestNG();
testng.setTestClasses(new Class<?>[] { TransferTests.class });
testng.addListener(new ScreenshotListener());
testng.run();

This is useful when a custom runner constructs the TestNG execution dynamically.

